docs {
  # Get Net Worth History

  Get the authenticated user's net worth for each day in a range, one series per currency.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/accounts/net-worth`

  ## Authentication

  This endpoint requires an active session. The session cookie must be included in the request (automatically sent by Bruno if you've signed in).

  ## Query Parameters

  - `range` (optional, default `1m`): how far back to go, counting back from today.
    - `1w`: 7 days
    - `1m`: 30 days
    - `3m`: 90 days
    - `1y`: 365 days
    - `all`: from the earliest day we have a balance for

  ## Response

  One series per currency (currencies are never added together), sorted by currency code. Each series has a point for every day from the start of the range to today, oldest first. A point's `date` is a UTC day (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and `netWorth` is everything owned minus everything owed (credit and loan balances are what is owed).

  - **Today** is the accounts' live balances, so the last point always equals what the accounts add up to now.
  - **Earlier days** come from the stored daily historic balances, per account. A day with no historic balance takes that account's latest earlier one; a day before its first historic balance takes the first (flat before the history starts). An account with no historic balances is held at its live balance throughout.
  - Accounts without a balance are left out. A user with no accounts gets an empty `series`.

  ## Success Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "range": "1w",
      "series": [
        {
          "currency": "CAD",
          "points": [
            { "date": "2026-10-03", "netWorth": 61200.5 },
            { "date": "2026-10-04", "netWorth": 61200.5 },
            { "date": "2026-10-10", "netWorth": 62589 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Error Responses

  - `400 Bad Request`: `range` is not one of the supported ranges
    ```json
    {
      "error": "Validation failed",
      "details": [{ "field": "range", "message": "Invalid enum value..." }]
    }
    ```

  - `401 Unauthorized`: No active session found

  ## Notes

  - The history before an item was linked is rebuilt from its transactions when it is first synced (investment accounts are held flat); see the webhooks service README.
}
